  "verbalization": "Ivosidenib is implicated in the treatment of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Ivosidenib is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation via two distinct routes. In one pathway, Ivosidenib is linked to Therapy Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia And Myelodysplastic Syndrome, which in turn is associated with Enasidenib, and Enasidenib is directly linked to Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation. In another pathway, Ivosidenib is linked to Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia, which is associated with Gilteritinib, and Gilteritinib is also linked to Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism where Ivosidenib may act through different molecular targets to influence the progression of this leukemia. The overlapping association with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation suggests that Ivosidenib may have a role in this disease, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated."
